<!--
  Windows Phone 8.1 Silverlight app.

  Structure follows the WP8.1 Silverlight C# project VS2015 ships (the
  PhoneSilverlightCS template) - project type guids, the Overrides/CSharp
  targets pair, and the AnyCPU/ARM/x86 configuration set are all taken from
  there rather than guessed.

  A pure managed app like this one normally builds AnyCPU and runs on both the
  emulator and the device. ARM and x86 exist for when a native component is
  added; x86 is the emulator, ARM the phone.

  Core\ is linked, not referenced: the same source compiles into the desktop
  harness, where the protocol is developed and debugged.
-->
